    "body": "<!-- crb-followup-result:v1 harvest=800 -->\n### Triage result\n\nEpic: #801\n\n- #802 [followups-800 01/16] Guard realtime test afterEach cleanup and cover the backpressure boundary\n- #803 [followups-800 02/16] Clarify ambiguous wording in the finish skill\n- #804 [followups-800 03/16] Thread actingUserId through createRelationProperty's invalidation\n- #805 [followups-800 04/16] Fix the adr-conventions skills-table row's threshold wording\n- #806 [followups-800 05/16] Reset reconnectAttempt when the sync client closes\n- #807 [followups-800 06/16] Fix the system status panel's summary class and its vacuous empty-state test\n- #808 [followups-800 07/16] Exclude in-flight jobs from the system health report's permanent count\n- #809 [followups-800 08/16] Assert response bodies for property.delete and view.delete contract tests\n- #810 [followups-800 09/16] Fix field extraction for union-schema validation errors in generic binding\n- #811 [followups-800 10/16] Cover ai-gateway shutdown drain timing and drop the unused poll-interval export\n- #812 [followups-800 11/16] Give the APNs config test's toThrow assertion a message pattern\n- #813 [followups-800 12/16] Name the fallback variable in the DATABASE_URL startup error\n- #814 [followups-800 13/16] Fix the agentRunsStore doc comment on userId requirement\n- #815 [followups-800 14/16] Cover docs.google.com URLs in the Gmail REST client test\n- #816 [followups-800 15/16] Remove the dead no-op block in the transcripts catalog migration\n- #817 [followups-800 16/16] Cover /internal/transcribe in the audio handler malformed-base64 test\n\n#### Rejected (8)\n\n| PR | Key | Verdict | Reason | Tracked by |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #395 | 90a77be3e4 | already-fixed | Commit 026a371 (\"Announce transcript computed writes from the data layer\") removed `runAfterCommit` from backend/packages/data/src/index.ts's export list and added `writeComputedAndAnnounce` as the encapsulating function instead, matching the finding's suggested fix; `runAfterCommit` no longer appears in the export list. |  |\n| #397 | bb8281cb53 | already-fixed | Commit 0bea54a (\"Cover remaining web bootstrap error branches\") added the test \"rejects a malformed failed query response as an API error\" to web/src/api/__tests__/authenticatedApiClient.test.ts, exercising the previously-uncovered non-401 error branch. |  |\n| #397 | adf58ef786 | already-fixed | The same commit 0bea54a added \"does not resolve an incomplete generic view URL\" and \"renders nothing when the view type has no registered renderer\" to GenericViewRoute.test.tsx, covering both previously-untested null-return branches. |  |\n| #399 | aeb5a19816 | already-fixed | Commit a503874 (\"Surface load-more failures instead of silently discarding them\") added setLoadMoreError(true) handling in both the failure-code branch and the catch block of handleLoadMore in LibraryGridViewContainer.tsx, plus a rendered error message. |  |\n| #399 | c878a00789 | already-fixed | The same commit a503874 added container and view tests covering the load-more failure path in LibraryGridViewContainer.test.tsx. |  |\n| #421 | 55275eebca | already-fixed | Commit 16a2e25 (\"Fix misleading no-deep-imports testSupport documentation\") renamed the test title in module-boundaries.unit.test.ts to accurately describe the hardcoded testSupport/ path exemption, removing the misleading \"package.json exports\" wording. |  |\n| #446 | ca24a188f3 | already-fixed | Commit 187c5cf (\"Address PR #446 review round 2 findings\") removed the `deriveTaskTime` export from backend/packages/data/src/index.ts since both internal callers already import it directly. |  |\n| #442 | 9f5ee92f21 | invalid | The finding claims CORE_TASK_NAMES.TRASH_PURGE gets no equivalent test, but PR #442 itself added an assertion for it in the \"includes the three inherited API-set names with affinity 'api'\" test in taskAffinity.unit.test.ts; the finding's premise is factually wrong. |  |\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=395 key=90a77be3e4 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=397 key=bb8281cb53 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=397 key=adf58ef786 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=399 key=aeb5a19816 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=399 key=c878a00789 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=421 key=55275eebca -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=446 key=ca24a188f3 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=442 key=9f5ee92f21 -->\n\n#### Advisories\n\nNone.\n",
